.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-3.0-or-later
.Dd November 20, 2026
.Dt NOQTIS-ARMOR 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm noqtis-armor
.Nd write a file as text (ASCII armor)
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm noqtis armor
.Op Fl l Ar label
.Op Fl o Ar out
.Op Fl -force
.Op Ar file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm noqtis armor
writes the bytes of
.Ar file ,
or of standard input when there is none or it is
.Ar - ,
as text that mail and a terminal carry (RFC 7468): a line
.Ql -----BEGIN label----- ,
the bytes in base64 in lines of 64 characters, and a line
.Ql -----END label----- .
The text is a third longer than the bytes and holds exactly them:
nothing is encrypted or signed by it.
A file of any length is armored, a line at a time.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl l Ar label , Fl -label Ns = Ns Ar label
The label: capitals and digits with single spaces between them, at
most 63 characters.
Default:
.Ql NOQTIS DATA .
.It Fl o Ar out , Fl -out Ns = Ns Ar out
The output file; standard output when it is not given or is
.Ar - .
.It Fl f , Fl -force
Replace an existing
.Ar out .
.El
.Pp
.Xr noqtis-sign 1
and
.Xr noqtis-box 1
write armor themselves with
.Fl a ,
under the labels
.Ql NOQTIS SIGNATURE
and
.Ql NOQTIS SEALED STREAM ,
and
.Xr noqtis-verify 1
and
.Xr noqtis-unbox 1
read it; a signature or a stream armored afterwards with the same label
is the same text.
Key files are text already
.Pq Xr noqtis-keygen 1 .
Do not armor a secret key with this command: its base64 is not
constant time.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when the text was written; 2 on a usage or file error.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal
$ printf 'hello, stream\en' | noqtis armor -l NOTE
-----BEGIN NOTE-----
aGVsbG8sIHN0cmVhbQo=
-----END NOTE-----
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-box 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-dearmor 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-sign 1 ,
.Xr nqarmenc 3
.Sh STANDARDS
.Rs
.%A S. Josefsson
.%A S. Leonard
.%T Textual Encodings of PKIX, PKCS, and CMS Structures
.%R RFC 7468
.%D April 2015
.Re
